.SS audit (how long the database copy is kept and where the durable log is shipped)
The stream has two sinks and they are not equals. The Logging destination below is the archive: one JSON line per event, unconditionally, for an external log system to ship and retain. The database table is a bounded cache that exists only to serve the web UI's recent\-history views, which is why it is pruned and deliberately not searchable beyond the two indexed subject columns.
.TP
.BI audit.retention: " duration"
How long an event stays in the database table. The scheduled sweep deletes rows older than this. It bounds the UI's history, not the deployment's: the shipped log is the archive, so a short window here loses nothing that matters. Zero disables age\-based pruning, leaving max_rows as the only bound.
Default:
.BR 1440h .
.TP
.BI audit.max_rows: " int"
Caps the table as a safety valve behind Retention, so a burst of events cannot grow it without bound inside the retention window. The same sweep deletes oldest\-first past the cap. The default is deliberately high: this exists to bound pathology, not to be the operative limit. Zero disables the cap.
Default:
.BR 1000000 .
.TP
.BI audit.sweep_interval: " duration"
How often the retention sweep runs. Pruning is not urgent \(em the window is measured in weeks \(em so this is measured in hours rather than minutes.
Default:
.BR 1h .
.TP
.B audit.logging.*
Log\-file rotation for this destination, via the embedded timberjack logger, with the same keys and meanings as logging.* above. This destination is only split out of the main log once its filename is set; until then its records go to the general log.
.TP
.BI audit.logging.level: " string"
The minimum log level for this destination, in the same form as logging.level.
Default:
.BR empty .
.TP
.BI audit.logging.add_source: " bool"
Includes the source file and line on each record.
Default:
.BR false .
.TP
.BI audit.logging.log_json: " bool"
Writes JSON instead of text. Text is meant to be read, not parsed: the message is written as bare prose so quoted values in it are not escaped, which is not a machine\-readable format. Set this wherever a log collector has to pull fields back out.
Default:
.BR true .
