.SS mail (the relay, the sender, and the local template overrides)
Disabled by default; see docs/operations/email\-notifications.md.  Disabled is the default. A server that has never been told about a relay should not try to reach one, and notifications are an addition to the certificate flows rather than a part of them \(em every path that emits one works identically when this is off.
.TP
.BI mail.enabled: " bool"
Turns outbound mail on. With it false the notification handler is not registered at all, so no event is queued and nothing is rendered.
