.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ISTERMINAL
Set to
.B 1
to force log output to be treated as an interactive terminal (colorized
text instead of plain/JSON), overriding real TTY detection on stderr.
Useful under a debugger or IDE-integrated terminal that isn't recognized as
a TTY. Not a general configuration mechanism: no other setting in this page
is read from the environment.
